  "contract": {
    "headers": "Eleven MMX/SSE/umbrella headers accept i386 and x64. AMX stays long-mode-only. The marker saves/restores the full EBX/RBX in the target width.",
    "hreset": "Both frontends emit effectful llvm.x86.hreset(i32), with all EAX bits and the ignored immediate canonically zero. Header wrappers use the same native builtin. Function target requirements remain hreset.",
    "capability": "__NEVERSIGHT_X86_HRESET__=1 indicates compiler API availability independently of TU CPU features. __has_builtin alone is feature-dependent and previously selected an unwanted assembly fallback even when the generated function had target(\"hreset\").",
    "neverd": "The shared native system inventory and C dispatch owner select HRESET in both modes. One feature-name owner now supplies LLVM and both C writers. Native calls reject weakened memory effects, speculation, noreturn, wrong calling convention and wrong architecture."
  },
