  "diagnosed_failures": [
    "The i386 frontend admitted source, but eleven packaged intrinsic headers still rejected its architecture; unconditional AMX declarations and a long-mode-only HRESET builtin also broke inclusion.",
    "The SSC marker used 64-bit registers in i386. Its target-width definition is now exercised in static/PIC code and also checks full-width RBX in x64.",
    "Clang exposed _hreset only through inline assembly. Its native builtin now uses the existing effectful LLVM API.",
    "Actual source compilation exposed feature-sensitive __has_builtin dispatch. A shared API capability fixes native selection with function-local target attributes.",
    "Initial fixture diagnostics are preserved: an incorrectly encoded HRESET test image, a constant-logical-operand test warning, and a standalone Clang linked before the rebuilt LLVM builtin lookup table."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "NeverC i386 is a Linux source frontend using full LLVM for objects; its embedded i386 machine backend/runtime is not restored.",
    "Controlled HRESET checks do not execute prediction-history reset and cannot establish its physical success, fault/event routing or machine-state continuations.",
    "The MMX header value tests do not close NeverD unowned/i386 MMX or x87 original-state lifter contracts.",
    "The wider original-machine, SMM/SGX, transaction, asynchronous-event and external-device boundaries remain as documented in x86-instruction-support.md."
  ],
